The `maxPresetColors === Infinity` check here is load-bearing in a non-obvious way. Without it, `Infinity` would pass `> 0` but fail `Number.isInteger` (which returns `false` for `Infinity`), causing a silent fallback to `27` instead of the intended "no limit" behavior. A brief inline comment would help future maintainers understand why the `Infinity` escape hatch must come before the `Number.isInteger` guard:
```ts
// Infinity fails Number.isInteger(), so it must be caught here explicitly
if (maxPresetColors === 0 || maxPresetColors === Infinity) {
```
